          "field": "trained horizon curves",
          "unit": "NLL per step"
        }
      ],
      "status": "consistent_directional_retrospective_evidence",
      "text": "Training with 1.0 s rather than current-token-only interaction input improved NLL by 0.004026 for the MLP and 0.003728 for the Transformer. All five paired groups had the preregistered direction, while exact multiplicity-adjusted tests remained underpowered; the 0.4 s condition captured nearly all of the gain."
    },
